{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וחזקהו", :translit "v'chazkeihu", :gloss "and strengthen him"} {:he "ב' דין", :translit "bet din", :gloss "bet: judgment"} {:he "החזק מלחמתך אל העיר והרסה", :translit "hachazeik milchamtecha el ha'ir v'aharseha", :gloss "strengthen your battle against the city and destroy it"} {:he "וחזקהו ביואב", :translit "v'chazkeihu b'Yo'av", :gloss "and strengthen him in Joab"} {:he "כמו שיואב היה שר צבא", :translit "k'mo she-Yo'av haya sar tzava", :gloss "just as Joab was commander of the army"} {:he "כך היה יהושע שר צבא", :translit "kach haya Yehoshua sar tzava", :gloss "so was Joshua commander of the army"} {:he "אף בחיי משה", :translit "af b'chayei Moshe", :gloss "even in Moses' lifetime"} {:he "כדי להחזיקו", :translit "k'dei l'chazeko", :gloss "in order to strengthen him"} {:he "כמו שמפורש במלחמת עמלק", :translit "k'mo she-mefurash b'milchemet Amaleik", :gloss "as is explicit in the war against Amalek"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling of וחזקהו with two bets signals two aspects: one of judgment/authority, one of military strength as in 2 Samuel."}], :frame {:text "The phrase וחזקהו appears with an extra bet, which Ba'al HaTurim reads as signaling a dual strengthening. Joshua served as military commander already during Moses' lifetime: when Moses ordered him to choose men and fight Amalek, he is described as doing so (Exodus 17:9–10, 13). The phrase החזק מלחמתך אל העיר והרסה is spoken by David to Joab in 2 Samuel 11:25, establishing the model of a commander who must be strengthened in battle.", :sources ["Exodus 17:9" "Exodus 17:10" "Exodus 17:13" "2 Samuel 11:25"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling of וחזקהו with two bets signals two aspects: one of judgment/authority, one of military strength as in 2 Samuel.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:49.789252335Z", :model "glm-5.2"}